WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:04.770
I'm Jenna Fisher.

2
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.070
And I'm Angela Kinsey.

3
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.370
We were on The Office together.

4
00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:08.610
And we're best friends.

5
00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:12.430
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.

6
00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:19.410
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.

7
00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:20.570
We're The Office ladies.

8
00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:26.940
And welcome to Conflict Resolution.

9
00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:29.660
I'm talking to you from my closet today.

10
00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:31.880
I know, we're both in our closets today.

11
00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:33.140
What is happening?

12
00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:37.340
We are both talking to each other from our closets.

13
00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:39.120
And Sam and Cody are watching.

14
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:40.760
I'm looking at Cody's cat.

15
00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:41.240
Love it.

16
00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:42.680
Sam's dog is somewhere there.

17
00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:45.020
This is where we're at now, folks.

18
00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:49.220
Angela, your shirts are very well folded.

19
00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:50.400
Are those Josh's shirts?

20
00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:51.260
No, baby girl.

21
00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:51.960
Baby girl.

22
00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:53.600
Are we doing that again this week?

23
00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:54.880
We are.

24
00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:55.800
Here's the thing.

25
00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:59.460
I've started every morning by talking to my family in Texas and Louisiana.

26
00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:02.480
And then it just is kind of with me for the whole day.

27
00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:06.500
This is my closet, my own closet.

28
00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:08.620
I share it with no one.

29
00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:10.620
It is a personal life victory.

30
00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:13.700
Oh my gosh, I only get one side of a closet.

31
00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:17.700
We have one closet and I get one side and Lee gets the other.

32
00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:24.300
Although, to be honest, I think I have encroached on about a third of his side.

33
00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:29.000
Well, Josh has his own closet, but one wall of it is my shoes.

34
00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:32.740
This is the riveting content that people tuned in for.

35
00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:33.400
I know.

36
00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:33.900
I know.

37
00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:36.660
Listen, but just bear with me one second.

38
00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:43.620
Here is a perk of not growing since like your junior year of high school.

39
00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:48.860
Maybe a little wider in some places, but I've had the same shoe size.

40
00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:52.020
Angela, you're describing most adults.

41
00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:57.880
I mean, most adults hit their peak height somewhere around their junior, senior year of high school.

42
00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:03.900
It's not like other people are continuing to grow four or five inches in their 20s and 30s.

43
00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:07.600
Do you have the same size foot as like when you were a sophomore?

44
00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:08.130
Yes, of course.

45
00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:08.680
You do?

46
00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:12.800
Yeah, I've been a seven and a half medium since like, you know, junior year of high school.

47
00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:15.060
I was fully grown when I went to college.

48
00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:15.980
I was fully grown.

49
00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:20.840
Oh, I unzipped my hoodie.

50
00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:21.480
Could y'all hear that?

51
00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:22.620
It sounded like a toot.

52
00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:24.300
It sounded like you tooted.

53
00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:24.508
What?

54
00:02:24.508 --> 00:02:25.080
It wasn't a toot.

55
00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:26.260
It sounded like a toot.

56
00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:30.400
It's good that you're claiming that you unzipped your hoodie.

57
00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:31.280
It was.

58
00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:32.320
Oh, my gosh.

59
00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:33.200
I see how it is.

60
00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:34.160
So we're here.

61
00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.680
It's Conflict Resolution Day, if you can't tell.

62
00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:43.020
It's season two, episode 21, written by Greg Daniels and directed by Charles McDougal.

63
00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:43.540
Action!

64
