00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:07.700
Scott Adsit is an amazing improviser, performer, comedian.

127
00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:10.020
You might know him from 30 Rock.

128
00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:12.480
Also, your children know him as Baymax.

129
00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:14.640
He's Baymax and Big Hero 6.

130
00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:16.700
Anyway, okay.

131
00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:17.900
That's my Baymax.

132
00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:19.620
Scott, you do it much better.

133
00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:24.760
So here's a little behind the scenes tidbit that he shared with me that he remembers from filming this episode.

134
00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:30.460
He said he remembers that Ricky Gervais came to visit set this week and everyone was abuzz.

135
00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:42.320
He said that Ricky seemed delighted and surprised by the scale of the production of our set and everything compared to maybe what his production of it had been like in the UK.

136
00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:45.660
And he said that Ricky was just very humble and sweet.

137
00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:46.460
Oh my gosh.

138
00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:49.740
I did not remember that Ricky visited during this episode.

139
00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:53.800
Yeah, I mean, he popped by in and out those first couple seasons, you know.

140
00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:58.560
But Scott remembered meeting him and he just said that he was just really nice.

141
00:05:58.680 --> 00:05:59.180
Oh my gosh.

142
00:05:59.260 --> 00:06:02.060
That's like a fast fact within a fast fact.

143
00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:02.720
What?

144
00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:04.320
That's a double fast fact.

145
00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:06.080
Did I help you get a double fast fact?

146
00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:06.700
You did.

147
00:06:06.980 --> 00:06:07.340
You did.

148
00:06:07.820 --> 00:06:11.400
Angela, I have a fun fact within this fast fact.

149
00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:16.520
Both you and Scott have appeared in two episodes of the TV show Monk.

150
00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:19.560
I was in one episode, yes, and I played the murderer.

151
00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:22.820
Well, Scott was on seasons three and four.

152
00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:27.880
So between the two of you, you cover four seasons of Monk.

153
00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:28.800
Congratulations.

154
00:06:29.440 --> 00:06:30.440
That's my fun fact.

155
00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:35.480
Monk was so much fun to shoot and Tony Shalhoub was the niceSt.

156
00:06:36.100 --> 00:06:42.620
We sat on like a little bench in between scenes and he was throwing something to try to get it in the trash can.

157
00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:46.440
And when it hit the trash can, it made like a ping-wong.

158
00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:49.020
And I started laughing and he started laughing.

159
00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:50.960
And I said, I mean, that was kind of a funny noise.

160
00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:57.560
And then the two of us sat there and did our impressions of the noises of things going in the trash can.

161
00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:07.640
Like, I don't know.

162
00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:09.420
He's just so fun.

163
00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:10.380
I just adored him.

164
00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:14.560
That fast fact was just chock full of fun and fast facts.

165
00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:16.460
That was a very full fast fact.

166
00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:18.160
It was a full fast fact.

167
00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:21.900
It was a full, fun, double fast fact.

168
00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:24.740
Fantastically fun, full fast fact.

169
00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:26.360
Oh, my gosh.

170
00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:27.920
Fast fact number two.

171
00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:29.020
Okay.

172
00:07:29.180 --> 00:07:32.280
Fast fact number two is a fan question from Zach Akers.

173
00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:35.100
And here's what he wrote in to say.

174
00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:48.740
Why does Jim do his talking heads in front of the outside facing window while everyone else's talking heads are inside of the window that faces the bullpen of the office?

175
00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:56.260
He says, in Booze Cruise and some later episodes, there are joint Jim-Pam talking heads in front of the outside window.

176
00:07:56.420 --> 00:08:01.360
But neither Pam nor anyone else normally sits in front of that outside window.

177
00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:09.140
And then he noticed, because Jim has several talking heads in this one, he was like, it's really prominent in this episode that Jim is there.

178
00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:16.760
So I thought that was a great question and such a wise observation I had to investigate.

179
00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:19.500
No, that is a great catch.

180
00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:20.560
It really is.

181
00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:25.940
So I emailed Greg Daniels and I asked him, was this deliberate?

182
00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:27.260
Was this an accident?

183
00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:29.240
What does he have to say?

184
00:08:29.420 --> 00:08:36.620
And he said that it was something that Randall Einhorn, our cinematographer, suggested to Greg, starting with the pilot.

185
00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:38.800
And Greg absolutely loved it.

186
00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:46.200
He said Randall's intention here was that it didn't necessarily have to be only Jim.

187
00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:59.600
But the idea was that any character that had a future outside of Dunder Mifflin or held some sort of internal optimism would sit in front of a window leading out into the world.

188
00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:11.360
But characters who didn't want to leave Dunder Mifflin or who maybe were in more of a position of being trapped would do their talking heads facing into the office.

189
00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:12.000
Wow.

190
00:09:12.220 --> 00:09:13.180
That's so deep.

191
00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:15.240
That's really deep.

192
00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:23.560
Yeah, I'm sitting here racking my brain to think of my character ever sat on that other wall with the window facing out behind her.

193
00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:29.780
And the one that comes to my mind, and I think it might be the only one I'm trying to think if there's any other one.

194
00:09:30.240 --> 00:09:33.480
It was when you and I did Big Pregs, Little Pregs.

195
00:09:33.580 --> 00:09:34.700
Yeah, we did.

196
00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:38.040
I think it's the only time I ever sat there.

197
00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:49.260
Well, for a very long time, I only sat there if I was with Jim, which was really the only possible future for Pam outside of the office.

198
00:09:50.260 --> 00:09:50.780
Wow.

199
00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:51.700
I think.

200
00:09:51.700 --> 00:09:52.300
That's so deep.

201
00:09:52.580 --> 00:09:53.440
Isn't that crazy?

202
00:09:53.620 --> 00:09:59.120
But otherwise, she was rather trapped in her, you know, bad decision of being with Roy.

203
00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:01.140
Trapped or content, you know?

204
00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:04.420
I mean, some of us were just happy with our lot in life.

205
00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:04.900
Yes.

206
00:10:04.900 --> 00:10:08.640
Um, well, that is fascinating, and I like it.

207
00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:10.500
Yeah, I thought that was a good one.

208
00:10:10.700 --> 00:10:14.380
So thank you so much, Zach, for pointing that out and writing in.

209
00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:20.300
Now, finally, fast fact number three, Angela, it's a fast fact flashback.

210
00:10:20.460 --> 00:10:21.360
What are you doing?

211
00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:22.120
What's up?

212
00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:22.840
Are you drunk?

213
00:10:23.660 --> 00:10:26.040
So here is this fast fact.

214
00:10:26.380 --> 00:10:29.380
This episode was filmed during May 2006.

215
00:10:29.380 --> 00:10:34.820
And so, Angela, my question for both of us is, what were you doing?

216
00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:39.380
Flashback now to May 2006, and what were you up to?

217
00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:45.720
Well, I had a journal entry from May 3rd, 2006.

218
00:10:45.800 --> 00:10:47.000
This is what I wrote.

219
00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:55.500
I wrote that I was doing a photo shoot with my cat, Lucy, for Cat Fancy Magazine.

220
00:10:55.940 --> 00:10:56.700
Angela Kinsey.

221
00:10:56.860 --> 00:10:57.080
What?

222
00:10:57.240 --> 00:10:58.480
Shut the front door right now.

223
00:10:58.560 --> 00:10:58.920
What?

224
00:10:59.060 --> 00:11:00.180
Do you know what I wrote in my journal?

225
00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:00.520
No.

226
00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:01.740
For this week of May.

227
00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:02.080
What?

228
00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:02.960
Of 2006.

229
00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:09.600
I did a photo shoot with my cat, Andy, for People Magazine.

230
00:11:09.740 --> 00:11:10.920
I'm not joking, lady.

231
00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:17.200
Lady, lady, how did we not know that we did photo shoots with our cats at this time?

232
00:11:19.230 --> 00:11:25.290
I feel like we probably at the time knew, but it's hilarious to me for us to both share

233
00:11:25.290 --> 00:11:31.290
our journal entries from early May 2006, and we were both so tickled that we were taking

234
00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:32.670
photos with our cats.

235
00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:34.290
Oh, my gosh.

236
00:11:34.450 --> 00:11:36.970
First of all, this is why we're BFFs, all right?

237
00:11:37.210 --> 00:11:37.890
This is why.

238
00:11:38.070 --> 00:11:41.830
Our life has very strange ways that it is parallel.

239
00:11:41.830 --> 00:11:44.870
So, was Lucy on the cover of Cat Fancy?

240
00:11:45.030 --> 00:11:48.330
No, Lucy was not on the cover because she was a rescue.

241
00:11:48.610 --> 00:11:50.370
She was not a purebred cat.

242
00:11:50.530 --> 00:11:54.450
But also, Jenna, Cat Fancy doesn't let humans on the cover.

243
00:11:55.810 --> 00:11:58.230
So, that's like, it's only cats on the cover.

244
00:11:58.370 --> 00:11:58.630
Okay.

245
00:11:58.790 --> 00:12:03.170
But the cool thing was is that Lucy and I got like, I think, I mean, I saved the magazine.

246
00:12:03.170 --> 00:12:04.810
I think we got like four pages.

247
00:12:05.090 --> 00:12:08.870
So, Lucy and I are in the center, I guess, for the centerfold.

248
00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:12.710
Oh, you are the centerfold of Cat Fancy magazine.

249
00:12:13.010 --> 00:12:14.530
So, Lucy and I look amazing.

250
00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:16.810
They're some of the best pictures I feel like I have.

