00:24:28.840 --> 00:24:29.600
Oh, I win.

502
00:24:29.600 --> 00:24:32.220
And I win, too, because I resolved it.

503
00:24:32.540 --> 00:24:34.720
And it's just, he's so good.

504
00:24:34.720 --> 00:24:41.700
Just in that very, like, small moment, you see how great he is at finessing all of these

505
00:24:42.440 --> 00:24:43.320
little moments.

506
00:24:43.440 --> 00:24:43.980
I love it.

507
00:24:44.060 --> 00:24:47.580
They should play that in acting schools as an example of moment of discovery.

508
00:24:47.800 --> 00:24:48.020
All right.

509
00:24:48.100 --> 00:24:52.600
So at four minutes, 32 seconds, they go over to, quote, look at the disputed poster.

510
00:24:52.860 --> 00:24:54.660
Michael wants them to express their feelings.

511
00:24:55.140 --> 00:24:58.840
And I say that the poster makes me happy.

512
00:24:59.600 --> 00:25:06.720
Because it makes me feel like the babies are the real artists, that God has a funny sense

513
00:25:06.720 --> 00:25:11.320
of humor and Oscar at five minutes, two seconds just goes off.

514
00:25:11.460 --> 00:25:13.220
And he has this rant.

515
00:25:13.420 --> 00:25:15.600
It was so fun to do this with Oscar.

516
00:25:15.760 --> 00:25:17.860
I have known him for so long.

517
00:25:17.860 --> 00:25:20.360
We performed together in sketch comedy.

518
00:25:20.360 --> 00:25:24.940
So I knew when they told him he could uncork what that meant.

519
00:25:24.940 --> 00:25:29.860
And it was just a delight for me when he was like, you know what?

520
00:25:30.060 --> 00:25:30.900
It's kitsch.

521
00:25:31.020 --> 00:25:32.160
It's the opposite of art.

522
00:25:32.320 --> 00:25:33.220
It destroys art.

523
00:25:33.380 --> 00:25:34.780
It destroys souls.

524
00:25:35.120 --> 00:25:36.900
Like, it just goes off.

525
00:25:36.900 --> 00:25:39.960
Was that improvised or scripted, Angela, or a mixture?

526
00:25:40.940 --> 00:25:42.080
It was a mixture.

527
00:25:42.260 --> 00:25:42.740
It was a mixture.

528
00:25:42.860 --> 00:25:44.820
And I think that was mostly scripted.

529
00:25:44.940 --> 00:25:50.240
But his stuff with Paul, with Toby in the conference room at the top of that scene was

530
00:25:50.240 --> 00:25:50.760
improvised.

531
00:25:50.920 --> 00:25:54.560
But Oscar is just so funny in this.

532
00:25:54.680 --> 00:25:57.160
And I just remember it was hard to keep a straight face.

533
00:25:57.160 --> 00:25:57.920
I remember that.

534
00:25:57.920 --> 00:26:01.180
But I had you to my right and Oscar to my left.

535
00:26:01.180 --> 00:26:02.300
It was very hard.

536
00:26:02.540 --> 00:26:05.340
It was very hard for me because Pam doesn't have any lines.

537
00:26:05.340 --> 00:26:09.180
And my direction was that I was not to react.

538
00:26:09.900 --> 00:26:13.480
I was to remain very neutral as possible.

539
00:26:13.820 --> 00:26:16.680
And so that was difficult to be neutral.

540
00:26:17.240 --> 00:26:17.900
All right.

541
00:26:17.960 --> 00:26:20.160
Well, we had a fan question from Zoe Kennedy.

